{
  "$comment": "Required attributes per product category, matched by category slug (case-insensitive). A category may have base 'attributes' (always shown) AND 'components' (optional sub-types). When no component is chosen the base attributes show; when a component is chosen its attributes REPLACE the base. Each attribute: name (slug, rendered as a data-cim-* product attribute), label, type (text|number|url|color|image|rfa|boolean|select), required, optional options (for select), optional default, optional disabled:true (shown but not editable). The CIM Revit plugin reads the data-cim-* DOM attributes verbatim (data-cim-tile-w etc.). Units follow the CIM spec: tile_w/tile_h in cm; else numeric in the unit named in its label. Component-tag fields (data-cim-tile-component / data-cim-paint-component) are locked to the exact Tile/Paint System component name the plugin validates against.",
